WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:27.140 align:start position:0%
 
come  uncharted the Nathan Drake collection is  a history lesson on a grand scale it  weaves through maps journals and diary  entries long separated from their  ancient authors and abandoned ruins  across the world but this collection  also delves into this series own dark  recesses highlighting the progress  developer Naughty Dog made from the  first uncharted to the third there is  brilliance in this collection but there  are hints of mediocrity as well  it begins in 2007 when we first met  Nathan Drake he since become a video  game icon but eight years ago he was  Naughty Dog's first departure from the  affable jak and daxter at the time Drake  had yet to prove his worth the Uncharted  series combines third-person action  cover based shooting and cinematic  storytelling across its three  installments we followed our hero across  deserts between mountains and  underground through ancient tombs by  grouping all 3 ps3 titles together in  one place the Nathan Drake collection  comprises a larger story arc we can  experience the entire original journey  from beginning to end in 1080p at 60  frames per second but this adventurers  early moments are unsettling despite its  upgrades the first Uncharted has not  aged well drake's Fortune used to be an  enjoyable accomplished game but that was  in 2007 it looks gorgeous now it's lush  jungles greener it's shooting controls  tighter thanks to Blue Point games  refinements but set against modern  standards its overall quality is  middling Drake's movements are floating  and imprecise the cover mechanic placed  me in danger far too often climbing  sequences leave little room for error  often leading to death for unknown  reasons there are even rare storytelling  missteps at the perceived death of his  closest friend  Drake allows himself a single gasp for  morning is displaced by excitement for  another adventure waiting through  Drake's first outing means suffering  constant frustrations but in the end  it's still worth playing because of what  its story leads to uncharted 2 among  thieves  fantastic sequels successfully  modernised by improved cosmetics and  smoother aiming controls Naughty Dog's  characters show real complexity here and  the relationships shift aligned and  resettle as the story takes haphazard  turns its pacing is masterful as ever -  in slower sections where other  developers might falter Naughty Dog uses  endearing dialogue and cinematic shots  to give the story a sense of gravity  there is as they say never a dull moment  much of the same rings true and  uncharted 3 drake's Deception  although the pacing stumbles throughout  and the story inch  reduces supernatural elements in a  predictable manner Naughty Dog's  characterization is at its peak here  Drake's bright personality shows darker  shades Sully tries to anchor things with  a warm comforting presence and Alana's  apprehension for Drake mirrors our own  as we grow to question his actions  during what we once thought was the  final leg of his journey but as of this  writing we know uncharted 3 isn't the  end uncharted 4 is on the way and with  it the continuation of drake's story and  preparing us for the vagabonds encore  likely his final chapter Blue Point  Games has delivered a polished prelude  it's created a singular story arc  leading into the fourth chapter and  polished it all for modern visual  palettes like the best stories those of  Uncharted and its characters have  changed over time the Nathan Drake  collection smooths out those crinkled  pages clarifies the memories and buffs  all the right details in the retelling  of the story series at various times  throughout the Uncharted games  our protagonist carries the ring of  Francis Drake on a leather band around  his neck the rings inscription reads SiC  parvis Magna or greatness from small  beginnings and I can't imagine a better  way to encapsulate this collection  uncharted drake's fortune was a fine  game in 2007 but its wrinkles are deeper  now it's age more apparent but with  uncharted 2 and three Naughty Dog  transcended Drake's own small beginnings  the Nathan Drake collection is a  first-hand account of Naughty Dog's  growth as a storyteller this collection  is the best way to relive that history  and witness that transformation up close  what do you say we try this again my  friends call me something  Nathan Drake not Drake  okay  I see great things in our future kid  great things  you

